.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::FluidCompressibilitySourceLHS< dim >"Volumetric source and sink terms that arise as the fluid expands or compresses due to pressure changes\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
this version uses sector-pore volume and total systems compressibilities of rocktypes that are associated with the elements\&.

.PP
fluid pressure is either taken from the node(FV) or interpolated with the finite-element interpolation to sector integration points\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::FluidCompressibilitySourceLHS\fP< dim >::AccumulateFiniteVolume (const \fBNode\fP< dim > & fv, \fBSparseMatrix\fP & mat) const\fR [virtual]\fP"
Since each sector of the finite volume may consist of a different rock type, the total systems compressibility must be summed up sector-by-sector, honouring the different contributions\&. 
.PP
.nf
@note using a single pressure value is perhaps not rigorous enough\&. One should rather interpolate
the pressure to the sector integration in order to capture the source term more accurately\&.

.fi
.PP
 
